<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=99=AB =E2=99=AA =F0=9F=8E=B5 =F0=9F=8E=
=B6 The champions =E2=99=AB =E2=99=AA =F0=9F=8E=B5 =F0=9F=8E=B6! <a href=3D=
"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyT=
NtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgd8nVGiq0DZ-Xd_86vbQV6tHYTAiDopF1al=
7WnzKTTVMVtziv8QD1Z4agZShBhUyFH6OFycf-8jYK4Zwvb1-fShP5BpbpPcYRwsUdjerpH3Ir-=
CA_VSnM4xIW3vZOhYOugiKdfXH_wnzY06SM3jXpioI8lnXBeb7LfXlfp-XQ-E20UBJtr4z7DvJR=
_pmTtBtA-fF6Po3jhgjLly3M-q2SambEK3tZ5wJ0PhH4alWl4fevWlHhu0tHuE9ICL-a45TD1Gd=
FR0MEdQkmX6JSciR5_w/4tv/5NtFoNZjT-iPh00QhCErNg/h29/h001.LbCLhOV_qE7_AqQVVH6=
Q8QmxrEKkzEUynoP0YX_Gr70" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Bigger Cup is back, bab=
y</a>! Red-hot action from the world=E2=80=99s premier club competition acr=
oss Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday. Bigger Vase and Tin Pot clubs must wai=
t for their slice of European action until after an international break alm=
ost as long as the Geopolitics World Cup itself. Rather like Gianni Infanti=
no=E2=80=99s North American investment roadshow, Bigger Cup, with its revol=
ving Swiss system, 36 teams reduced to 24 following 114 matches, has become=
 baggier than MC Hammer=E2=80=99s trousers [now there=E2=80=99s a reference=
 for the young readers =E2=80=93 Football Daily Ed]. Back in Clive Tyldesle=
y=E2=80=99s ITV pomp, ties such as Liverpool v Atl=C3=A9tico, Napoli v Arse=
nal, and Real Madrid v Inter moved the dial, filling boozers and column inc=
hes.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Now, paywalled away and despite the whir o=
f Darren Fletcher and Ally McCoist=E2=80=99s unrelenting hype machine, thes=
e nights can feel more routine, a golden goose not so much terminated as ga=
thering dust on the mantelpiece. A trinket retaining monetary value but not=
 as cherished as it once was. That holders PSG are so minted they can affor=
d to play separate teams across Ligue 1 and Bigger Cup says much about mode=
rn football, where clubs and competitions have become content providers fee=
ding an attention economy. In this case, that attention will run a deficit =
until, just like the GWC, the juice is in the knockout stages. There are, t=
hough, different dimensions to take solace in.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Uefa suits would argue, for all the ennui =
surrounding Manchester City facing Real Madrid 14 times since 2012 =E2=80=
=93 they don=E2=80=99t meet in this year=E2=80=99s group =E2=80=93 Bigger C=
up offers pluralism in the presence of minnows and newcomers. Think of them=
 like plucky non-league clubs in the FA Cup third round. There=E2=80=99s Se=
rie A arrivistes Como, a cracking away trip for fans, with Cesc F=C3=A0breg=
as as well-regarded young coach, and Nico Paz as a potential successor to L=
ionel Messi. No pressure. Austria=E2=80=99s Lask, from Linz, will make thei=
r group stage debut, having <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian=
.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0B=
xnPgbJTN3jrgVl0qfftxoCXgiHb8V6AYg0jhwU3OgZu2lehjhryvns-II0tP-boBQNiH9L-i4JM=
UW6VnTwgqB9dNutxFoD1ARdsb-zyKAzdGG3ARrjLeKs4xLV3M6LGh8dZC1TS1rupLlMkNvO--Mu=
Ds6aUDSh8vGrdJUaTIz5VGuP3ja5RAF2csyfR2HeUcjnDq/4tv/5NtFoNZjT-iPh00QhCErNg/h=
30/h001.khHdHzPlrz46XJYcYXAVi1hDKN2KHVZq17aAUs87Sfo" style=3D"color: #0077B=
6;">sunk Celtic in the playoffs</a> and featuring the talents of former Man=
gotsfield, Wealdstone, Yeovil, Chesterfield, Swindon and St Mirren defender=
 Miguel Freckleton.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Azerbaijani football has previously been r=
epresented by Qarabag but Sabah are the new Azeri force, from a small munic=
ipality on the banks of the Masazir, an actual salt lake. Their coach, Vald=
as Dambrauskas, will be reunited with Manchester United. Using the funds fr=
om a small, Who Wants To Be A Millionaire win on Lithuanian TV in 2002, hav=
ing phoned a friend, gone 50-50 and asked the audience, he emigrated to Eng=
land, eventually becoming a coach at United=E2=80=99s soccer schools in 200=
4, beginning his long personal journey back to Old Trafford. Then there=E2=
=80=99s Slovan Bratislava, coached by a 2009 Big Cup winner in Yaya Tour=C3=
=A9, who succeeded Vladimir Weiss in the summer. Tour=C3=A9 becomes the fir=
st African coach to lead a team in the competition=E2=80=99s group stage, e=
nding a wait that has lasted far too long. Throw in the return of Bod=C3=B8=
/Glimt and questions of whether the club from the Arctic Circle can keep on=
 doing interesting things and not everybody has to be a billionaire=E2=80=
=99s plaything, though come the spring, it will certainly help.</p>
